WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.292 --> 00:00:02.060
HURRICANE MARIA.

00:00:00.792 --> 00:00:03.795
TONIGHT WE CONTINUE TO LOOK AT

00:00:02.193 --> 00:00:04.095
THE RECOVERY OR LACK OF IT

00:00:03.928 --> 00:00:06.197
THERE.

00:00:04.229 --> 00:00:08.300
CORRESPONDENT BRYAN LLENAS IS AN

00:00:06.331 --> 00:00:11.503
OLD SAN JUAN WITH THE STORY.

00:00:08.433 --> 00:00:12.070
&gt;&gt; WE ARE TREATED AS

00:00:11.636 --> 00:00:14.072
SECOND-CLASS CITIZENS.

00:00:12.203 --> 00:00:14.472
&gt;&gt; PUERTO RICO GOVERNOR IS

00:00:14.205 --> 00:00:15.940
FRUSTRATED.

00:00:14.606 --> 00:00:17.275
HE SAID THE HURRICANE MARIA

00:00:16.074 --> 00:00:19.411
DISASTER FUNDS ARE TAKING TOO

00:00:17.409 --> 00:00:19.778
LONG TO ARRIVE AND HE BLAMES

00:00:19.544 --> 00:00:21.613
CONGRESS.

00:00:19.911 --> 00:00:23.515
&gt;&gt; WHY IS THE SAME COP PROCESS

00:00:21.746 --> 00:00:25.183
IN FLORIDA OR TEXAS, IT TAKES A

00:00:23.648 --> 00:00:25.517
WEEK, AND PUERTO RICO, IT TAKES

00:00:25.317 --> 00:00:27.118
MONTHS.

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:29.954
&gt;&gt; HE IS NOT ALONE.

00:00:27.252 --> 00:00:30.689
ON TUESDAY, NEARLY TWO DOZEN

00:00:30.088 --> 00:00:32.724
PUERTO RICAN ACTIVISTS WERE

00:00:30.822 --> 00:00:34.326
ARRESTED IN THE U.S. CAPITAL

00:00:32.857 --> 00:00:35.727
DEMANDING CONGRESS PROVIDE MORE

00:00:34.459 --> 00:00:36.494
FINANCIAL AID TO THE

00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:39.197
COMMONWEALTH.

00:00:36.628 --> 00:00:40.198
PUERTO RICO CLAIMS THAT NEEDS

00:00:39.331 --> 00:00:42.534
$94 BILLION IN AID.

00:00:40.332 --> 00:00:44.202
CONGRESS APPROPRIATED

00:00:42.667 --> 00:00:44.669
23 BILLION, LESS THAN 2 BILLION

00:00:44.336 --> 00:00:46.971
HAS BEEN SENT.

00:00:44.803 --> 00:00:48.206
&gt;&gt; I WANT TO SEE SHOVELS IN THE

00:00:47.105 --> 00:00:50.675
GROUND AND THINGS BEING BUILT.

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:53.845
HOUSES BEING BUILT TO CODE.

00:00:50.809 --> 00:00:55.647
I WANT TO SEE A POWER SYSTEM

00:00:53.978 --> 00:00:56.848
THAT'S UNDER CONSTRUCTION THAT

00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:59.050
WILL WITHSTAND A STORM.

00:00:56.981 --> 00:01:00.051
&gt;&gt; MICA SAYS FEMA'S EFFORTS HAS

00:00:59.184 --> 00:01:01.886
BEEN UNLIKE ANY HURRICANE

00:01:00.185 --> 00:01:05.256
RESPONSE HE HAS SEEN, SPENDING

00:01:02.020 --> 00:01:06.691
MORE THAN $6 BILLION SO FAR.

00:01:05.390 --> 00:01:07.325
$15 MILLION HAS GONE TO SAN

00:01:06.825 --> 00:01:10.395
SEBASTIAN, WHERE THE MAYOR

00:01:07.459 --> 00:01:13.365
BLAMES SAN JUAN, NOT THE FEDS.

00:01:10.528 --> 00:01:15.100
&gt;&gt; THIS TOWN TOOK CONTROL OF OUR

00:01:13.498 --> 00:01:15.533
CIRCUMSTANCES AND RELISTED

00:01:15.233 --> 00:01:16.634
OURSELVES UP.

00:01:15.667 --> 00:01:18.503
&gt;&gt; FRUSTRATED AFTER NOT SEEING

00:01:16.768 --> 00:01:20.638
POWER RESTORED IN A MONTH, THE

00:01:18.636 --> 00:01:21.439
TOWN CREATED VOLUNTEER BRIGADES,

00:01:20.772 --> 00:01:22.507
INCLUDING RETIRED LINEMAN TO

00:01:21.573 --> 00:01:24.809
RESTORE POWER AND CLEAR DEBRIS

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:27.412
ON THEIR OWN.

00:01:24.943 --> 00:01:27.879
HE SAYS THE PROBLEM IS IN FEMA

00:01:27.545 --> 00:01:28.947
FUNDING.

00:01:28.012 --> 00:01:30.248
&gt;&gt; THE GOVERNOR SHOULD HAVE

00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:32.283
ACTED WITH MORE URGENCY.

00:01:30.382 --> 00:01:33.284
HE SHOULD HAVE TAKEN CHARGE OF

00:01:32.417 --> 00:01:34.753
THE UTILITY COMPANY.

00:01:33.418 --> 00:01:35.487
IMMEDIATELY FIRING THOSE WHO

00:01:34.886 --> 00:01:37.689
WEREN'T DOING THEIR JOBS.

00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:39.357
&gt;&gt; ON TUESDAY THE GOVERNOR

00:01:37.822 --> 00:01:40.658
APPOINTED A NEW HEAD OF THE

00:01:39.491 --> 00:01:42.594
BANKRUPT GOVERNMENT ON POWER

00:01:40.792 --> 00:01:44.095
UTILITY WIDELY BLAMED FOR THE

00:01:42.727 --> 00:01:44.696
ISLANDS FEELING ELECTRIC

00:01:44.229 --> 00:01:46.131
INFRASTRUCTURE.

00:01:44.829 --> 00:01:48.500
5,000 BUSINESSES ARE NOW CLOSED

00:01:46.264 --> 00:01:49.768
AND EXPECTING TO NEVER REOPEN.

00:01:48.633 --> 00:01:51.436
JOHNNY RAMOS, PRESIDENT OF A

00:01:49.901 --> 00:01:52.370
MANUFACTURING COMPANY, SAYS TIME

00:01:51.569 --> 00:01:55.774
IS RUNNING OUT.

00:01:52.504 --> 00:01:56.441
&gt;&gt; I CANNOT SIT DOWN AND WAIT

00:01:55.907 --> 00:01:58.042
FOR THE GOVERNMENT.

00:01:56.574 --> 00:02:00.645
I HAVE TO MOVE.

00:01:58.176 --> 00:02:02.046
&gt;&gt; COMPOUNDING THE CRISES,

00:02:00.779 --> 00:02:02.714
PUERTO RICO IS BANKRUPT.

00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:03.648
TOMORROW TREASURY SECRETARY

00:02:02.847 --> 00:02:05.283
STEVE MNUCHIN WILL BE TO THE

00:02:03.782 --> 00:02:07.318
GOVERNOR HERE IN OLD SAN JUAN TO

00:02:05.417 --> 00:02:08.052
SECURE THE TERMS FOR A

00:02:07.452 --> 00:02:09.854
$2 BILLION DEAL.

00:02:08.186 --> 00:02:13.491
HE SAYS HE WANTS TO ENTER

